<title>UK: UK's Clarke says budget to tighten fiscal policy.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke says budget to tighten fiscal policy.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said his annual budget was aimed at tightening fiscal policy to reduce the risk of higher interest rates.</p>
<p>&quot;This budget tightens fiscal policy. I am tightening fiscal policy now to reduce the risk of having to tighten monetary policy excessilvely as I set policy to hit my inflation target,&quot; Clarke said in a speech to parliament on the 1997/98 budget.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
